/* Extra scheme subjects and higher-order challenge questions for Catch-Up Club. */
window.EXTRA_SUBJECTS = [
 ["Biology","🧬","Human growth and development","Drugs",[
  ["Human growth and development","Growth is a measurable increase in body size, while development is the gradual gaining of new abilities and maturity. Puberty is a stage of development when hormones cause physical and emotional changes. People do not all develop at the same age or rate. Respectful language, reliable information and support from a trusted adult matter."],
  ["Drugs and the body","A drug is a substance that changes how the body or mind works. Medicines are drugs used carefully to prevent or treat illness. The effect depends on the substance, amount, route into the body and the person. Misusing medicines or using harmful substances can affect the brain, heart, lungs, liver, judgement and relationships. Never take an unknown substance; ask a trusted adult or health professional."],
  ["Habitats and ecosystems","A habitat is the place where an organism lives. An ecosystem includes the living community and the non-living conditions interacting in an area. Producers make food, consumers obtain energy by eating organisms, and decomposers break down dead material and return nutrients. A change to one population can affect the food web and the balance of the whole ecosystem."],
  ["How to answer Biology questions","Use precise terms and link structure to function. In a process question, write events in order and explain cause and effect. In a comparison, state a similarity or difference on both sides. In an investigation, identify the variable changed, the outcome measured and the conditions kept the same."]
 ],[
  ["Which statement correctly distinguishes growth from development?","Growth is measurable increase in size; development is gaining abilities and maturity.",["They are exactly the same process","Growth is measurable increase in size; development is gaining abilities and maturity.","Development only means becoming taller","Growth only happens after puberty"],1],
  ["A student measures the time taken for food to leave the stomach after different meals. What is the dependent variable?","The time taken for food to leave the stomach",["The meal type","The time taken for food to leave the stomach","The student’s age","The measuring clock"],1],
  ["Why can removing a predator cause a prey population to rise at first?","Fewer prey are eaten, so more survive to reproduce.",["The prey turn into producers","Fewer prey are eaten, so more survive to reproduce.","All plants immediately disappear","Predators make prey reproduce"],1]
 ]],
 ["Chemistry","⚗️","History and development of the atomic model","Weather, climate and ice ages",[
  ["Solutions and dissolving","A solution is a uniform mixture made when a solute dissolves in a solvent. Salt is the solute and water is the solvent in salt water. Dissolving does not destroy the particles; they spread through the liquid. Stirring and heating usually increase the rate of dissolving, while temperature and the identity of the substances affect how much can dissolve."],
  ["Solubility and concentration","Solubility is the maximum amount of a solute that dissolves in a stated amount of solvent at a stated temperature. A saturated solution contains as much dissolved solute as it can hold at that temperature. Concentration describes how much solute is present in a given volume of solution; concentration = mass ÷ volume when the units are consistent."],
  ["Pure substances and separation","A pure substance contains one substance and has characteristic properties. Mixtures contain substances physically combined. Filtration separates an insoluble solid from a liquid; evaporation or crystallisation recovers a dissolved solid; chromatography separates soluble colours because they move different distances with a solvent. Diffusion is the net spreading of particles from a region of higher concentration to lower concentration."],
  ["Atoms and models","Atoms contain a tiny, dense, positively charged nucleus with protons and neutrons, surrounded by negatively charged electrons in shells. In a neutral atom, proton number equals electron number. Electron arrangements for the first 20 elements are filled 2, then 8, then 8, then 2. Models are useful explanations but can change when new evidence appears."],
  ["Energy changes and metal reactions","An exothermic reaction transfers energy to the surroundings, so the surroundings warm. An endothermic reaction takes in energy, so the surroundings cool. A more reactive metal can displace a less reactive metal from its compound. Metals reacting with acids may produce a salt and hydrogen; describe observations and use a splint test only with teacher supervision."],
  ["Weather and climate","Weather describes short-term atmospheric conditions; climate describes long-term patterns. Temperature, rainfall, wind, humidity and air pressure are measured with different instruments. Climate is affected by latitude, altitude, distance from the sea and prevailing winds. Ice ages are long periods when global temperatures and ice coverage differ greatly from today; climate evidence must be interpreted over long timescales."],
  ["How to answer Chemistry questions","Show working and units in calculations. Separate an observation (what you see or measure) from an explanation (particle or energy model). For chromatography, identify the solvent and compare how far each dye travels. For reactions, state reactants, products, evidence and the energy transfer."]
 ],[
  ["At a fixed temperature, 20 g of salt dissolves in 100 g of water. What happens when 25 g is added and all the salt is stirred?","A saturated solution forms and about 5 g remains undissolved.",["All 25 g must dissolve because stirring increases solubility","A saturated solution forms and about 5 g remains undissolved.","The salt changes into water","The solution becomes pure water"],1],
  ["A solution contains 12 g of solute in 0.40 dm³. What is its concentration in g/dm³?","30 g/dm³",["4.8 g/dm³","30 g/dm³","0.033 g/dm³","12.4 g/dm³"],1],
  ["An atom has 11 protons and 10 electrons. What is its charge and electron arrangement?","+1; 2,8",["Neutral; 2,8,1","+1; 2,8","−1; 2,8","+11; 10"],1],
  ["A blue dye travels 6 cm while the solvent front travels 8 cm. What is its Rf value?","0.75",["1.33","0.75","14","2"],1],
  ["Metal X displaces metal Y from Y sulfate, but Y cannot displace X from X sulfate. What can be concluded?","X is more reactive than Y.",["Y is more reactive than X","X is more reactive than Y.","Both have equal reactivity","Neither metal reacts"],1],
  ["A reaction mixture becomes colder without external cooling. Which energy change best explains this?","The reaction is endothermic and takes in energy from its surroundings.",["The reaction is exothermic and releases energy","The reaction is endothermic and takes in energy from its surroundings.","No energy is transferred","The thermometer creates energy"],1]
 ]],
 ["Yoruba","🗣️","Àwọn Iṣẹ́-ìṣẹ̀ńbáyé (traditional occupations)","Àkàyé (comprehension)",[
  ["Ìṣẹ̀dá Ọ̀rọ̀ Orúkọ: nominalisation","Nominalisation is forming or using a noun from another word or expression. In Yoruba, examine the word in its sentence: ask whether it names a person, place, thing, action or idea. Learn the exact forms taught in class because tone marks and word boundaries can change meaning."],
  ["Numbers and meaning","The scheme practises counting from 101 to 500. Read number expressions carefully, recognise the hundreds and tens, and practise both speaking and writing. Check the pattern and pronunciation with your class model; Yoruba tone marks are meaningful and should not be dropped when copying vocabulary."],
  ["Traditional occupations","An occupation is work people do to earn a living or provide useful goods and services. Traditional occupations can include farming, fishing, weaving, pottery, blacksmithing, trading and carving. Learn the Yoruba names given in class, what each worker produces, the tools used and how the work supports a community."],
  ["Àkàyé: reading comprehension","Read the passage once for its main idea and again for details. Use the passage as evidence, answer in a complete sentence, and do not add information that the passage does not support. For Yoruba answers, retain correct spelling and tone marks from the text."],
  ["Lítíréṣò Alohùn: oral literature","Oral literature is literature spoken, sung or performed and passed on by speaking rather than only through print. Examples may include folktales, proverbs, praise poetry, chants and songs. Discuss the performer, audience, language, repetition, imagery, lesson and cultural setting using the examples studied in class."],
  ["Yoruba accuracy checklist","Check tone marks, vowel dots, word spacing and meaning. When a task asks for a translation, preserve the sense of the whole sentence rather than translating word by word. Use your teacher’s class vocabulary for occupations and number forms; the scheme provides headings, not a full word list."]
 ],[
  ["A passage says a farmer sells yam at the market. Which answer is best supported?","The farmer uses farming to provide food for the community.",["The farmer is a doctor","The farmer uses farming to provide food for the community.","The farmer lives beside the sea","The farmer makes metal tools"],1],
  ["What makes an answer to àkàyé well supported?","It uses details from the passage and answers the question directly.",["It adds a guess from outside the passage","It uses details from the passage and answers the question directly.","It copies an unrelated sentence","It omits the main idea"],1],
  ["Which is the strongest way to revise traditional occupations?","Connect each class-taught Yoruba name to the worker, tools and products.",["Memorise only English job titles","Connect each class-taught Yoruba name to the worker, tools and products.","Guess tone marks","Study occupations without examples"],1],
  ["Why should Yoruba tone marks be copied carefully?","They can distinguish pronunciation and meaning.",["They are decoration only","They can distinguish pronunciation and meaning.","They replace every vowel","They show a word is plural"],1]
 ]]
];

