 History:[["A source was written by a government official during a conflict. What is the most careful first judgement?","It may give valuable contemporary evidence, but perspective and purpose must be considered.",["It is automatically false","It may give valuable contemporary evidence, but perspective and purpose must be considered.","It is neutral because it is official","It proves every event"],1],["Why does a timeline help explain the 1966 coups and later conflict?","It distinguishes sequence and helps assess how events may be connected.",["It replaces evidence","It distinguishes sequence and helps assess how events may be connected.","It guarantees one cause","It removes dates"],1],["How should a student explain reconciliation after war?","Describe efforts to rebuild trust and unity, using a policy or example as evidence.",["Only list weapons","Describe efforts to rebuild trust and unity, using a policy or example as evidence.","Say rebuilding roads is the same as reconciliation","Ignore affected people"],1]],
